---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CautionPanel from "../components/CautionPanel.astro";
import CommandStep from "../components/CommandStep.astro";
import EvidenceFigure from "../components/EvidenceFigure.astro";
import LeverButton from "../components/LeverButton.astro";
import Lockup from "../components/Lockup.astro";
import Plate from "../components/Plate.astro";
import StatusLamp from "../components/StatusLamp.astro";
import TrackSection from "../components/TrackSection.astro";
import brokerOverview from "../assets/hmi-overview.webp";
import mqttUsers from "../assets/hmi-users.webp";
import deployPanel from "../assets/hmi-deploy.webp";

const repoURL = "https://github.com/fgjcarlos/mcm";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");

const quickStart = [
  { label: "Clone and build", code: "git clone https://github.com/fgjcarlos/mcm.git && cd mcm && task build" },
  { label: "Start the development stack", code: "task up" },
  { label: "Find the initial administrator sign-in", code: "task logs    # first-boot credentials are printed here when generated" },
];

const stack = ["Go 1.25", "SQLite", "Mosquitto", "React 19 + Vite 8", "REST + WebSocket API"];
---

<Layout
  title="MCM — Mosquitto Control Manager"
  description="MCM is a self-hosted administration interface for an existing Mosquitto broker. See what is available in the alpha and try it locally."
>
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-6 pb-16">
    <header>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-8 gap-y-4 border-b border-track py-5">
        <Lockup />
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <Plate variant="lamp">Alpha</Plate>
          <Plate>Apache 2.0</Plate>
          <a class="link text-sm text-enamel-soft" href={`${repoURL}/actions/workflows/ci.yml`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Image CI workflow</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-4xl pt-16 sm:pt-24">
        <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold uppercase leading-[0.92] text-enamel-bright sm:text-7xl lg:text-[5.5rem]">Manage a Mosquitto broker from the web.</h1>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft sm:text-xl">
          Mosquitto is the server that routes MQTT messages between devices. MCM adds a browser interface and API to manage one Mosquitto broker; Mosquitto continues to handle the messages.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] leading-relaxed text-enamel">Alpha: useful configuration controls are available today, while the graphical configuration interface is still incomplete.</p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <LeverButton href="#quick-start">
            Try locally
            <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="size-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M8 2v11M3 8.5l5 5 5-5" /></svg>
          </LeverButton>
          <LeverButton href={repoURL} variant="ghost" external>GitHub</LeverButton>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <TrackSection class="mt-28 sm:mt-36" titleId="availability-title" title="What you can change today—and what remains.">
      <p slot="lede">The current alpha manages one Mosquitto broker. The available controls are real; coverage and production readiness are not complete.</p>
      <div class="grid divide-y divide-track lg:grid-cols-3 lg:divide-x lg:divide-y-0">
        <article class="pb-8 lg:pb-0 lg:pr-8">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-enamel-bright">Available controls</h3>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-enamel">Who can connect:</span> MQTT users and access control rules.</li>
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-enamel">What the broker exposes:</span> listeners and TLS certificates.</li>
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-enamel">What it carries:</span> general settings and bridges.</li>
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-enamel">What it extends:</span> plugins including Dynamic Security, and editing the main <code>mosquitto.conf</code> file.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">Applying changes requires a fresh multi-factor authentication (MFA) check: enter a new code from your authenticator app.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="py-8 lg:px-8 lg:py-0">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-enamel-bright">Remaining work</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">Native ACL coverage is still partial. Five directives per supported version are validated and preserved but edited only in the advanced root editor, and the included files of an <code>include_dir</code> tree are read but not edited. The <a class="link" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/support-matrix.md`}>support matrix</a> lists the exact coverage of every Mosquitto version.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pt-8 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-enamel-bright">Known limitations</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">SQLite is the only implemented management database. Observed traffic is not a full client inventory. Sparkplug B and JSON Schema diagnostics inspect messages for issues but never block or reject them.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <details class="mt-12 border-y border-track py-5">
        <summary class="font-display text-lg font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-enamel marker:text-enamel-muted">Detailed scope</summary>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">Fleets, multi-broker management, single sign-on (SSO), high availability, and PostgreSQL are deferred.</p>
      </details>
    </TrackSection>

    <TrackSection class="mt-28 sm:mt-36" titleId="evidence-title" title="Review, apply, verify.">
      <p slot="lede">Real captures from a running MCM local stack. Select any image to inspect its full-size file. The dashboard also has a Broker diagnostics workspace reporting the broker's own view of connections, logs and metrics.</p>
      <EvidenceFigure
        image={deployPanel}
        alt="MCM deploy panel showing configuration preview controls and deployment history with a verified activation entry."
        openLabel="Open full-size MCM deploy panel capture"
      >
        <p>Deploy panel: preview configuration changes before applying them. Sensitive changes require a fresh authenticator code.</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
          <li><StatusLamp status="verified">Verified activation:</StatusLamp> the probe confirmed the change took effect.</li>
          <li><StatusLamp status="rolled-back">Rolled back deployment:</StatusLamp> the change was reverted because the activation could not be confirmed.</li>
          <li><StatusLamp status="failed">Failed apply:</StatusLamp> the apply failed and the previous configuration was restored.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">These records show both recovery paths, not only successful deployments.</p>
        <details class="mt-3">
          <summary class="text-enamel">Why the outcomes occurred</summary>
          <p class="mt-1">Entry 3 was verified by a user-grant probe. Entry 2 rolled back because the configured managed service account lacked a user read/write grant, so no activation probe was available. Entry 1 failed during apply and restored the saved snapshot.</p>
        </details>
        <a class="link mt-3 inline-block" href={deployPanel.src}>Open full-size capture</a>.
      </EvidenceFigure>
      <div class="mt-16 grid gap-12 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-8">
        <EvidenceFigure
          image={brokerOverview}
          alt="MCM broker overview showing connection status, observed message rate and top topics."
          openLabel="Open full-size broker overview capture"
        >
          Broker overview: check the broker connection status, observed message rate, and top topics. Observed messages are not a complete client inventory. <a class="link" href={brokerOverview.src}>Full-size</a>.
        </EvidenceFigure>
        <EvidenceFigure
          image={mqttUsers}
          alt="MCM MQTT user directory showing user status and controls to disable an account or reset its password."
          openLabel="Open full-size MQTT user directory capture"
        >
          MQTT user directory: check account status and available controls to disable a user or reset their password. <a class="link" href={mqttUsers.src}>Full-size</a>.
        </EvidenceFigure>
      </div>
    </TrackSection>

    <CautionPanel class="mt-28 sm:mt-36" titleId="production-title" title="Alpha software; review production limits before applying changes.">
      <p>The configuration journey is implemented and verified against a real Mosquitto, but some directives have no dedicated control and MCM is still alpha. Review the deployment requirements before enabling writes on an existing broker.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold text-enamel">
        <a class="link" href={`${repoURL}/issues/308`}>Configuration tracker</a>
        <a class="link" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/support-matrix.md`}>Directive support matrix</a>
        <a class="link" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/product-scope.md`}>Scope and acceptance criteria</a>
        <a class="link" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/production.md#current-limitations`}>Production limitations</a>
      </div>
    </CautionPanel>

    <details class="mt-12 border-y border-track py-5">
      <summary class="font-display text-lg font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-enamel marker:text-enamel-muted">Technical stack</summary>
      <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {stack.map((item) => <li class="border border-track-strong px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-enamel">{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-enamel-muted">MCM's application includes the dashboard and management API; Mosquitto runs separately. SQLite is the only implemented management database.</p>
    </details>

    <TrackSection class="mt-28 sm:mt-36" id="quick-start" titleId="quick-start-title" title="Run the alpha locally.">
      <p slot="lede">For this local development setup, install <a class="link" href="https://git-scm.com/downloads">Git</a> to clone the source, <a class="link" href="https://docs.docker.com/compose/install/">Docker Compose</a> to run the containers, and <a class="link" href="https://taskfile.dev/installation/">Task</a> to run the project commands. These steps start a development stack, not a production deployment.</p>
      <ol>
        {quickStart.map((step, idx) => (
          <CommandStep n={idx + 1} label={step.label} code={step.code}>
            {idx === quickStart.length - 1 && (
              <Fragment>
                <div class="border-t border-track pt-6">
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-enamel-bright">Success checkpoint</h3>
                  <ol class="mt-3 list-inside list-decimal space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft marker:font-mono marker:text-enamel-muted">
                    <li>Open <a class="link font-mono text-enamel" href="http://localhost:8080">http://localhost:8080</a>.</li>
                    <li>Sign in with the generated credentials from the first-start logs, or the administrator credentials configured before first start.</li>
                    <li>Confirm the dashboard shows the broker as connected.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 border-t border-track pt-6 md:grid-cols-3">
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-enamel-bright">No bootstrap credentials in the logs?</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">There is no default password. If no generated credentials appear, check whether <code class="wrap-anywhere">MCM_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME</code> and <code class="wrap-anywhere">MCM_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> were set before first start, then use those values. Do not guess or reuse a broker password.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-enamel-bright">Signed in, but the broker shows disconnected?</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">In the dashboard you just opened, go to Diagnostics → Broker diagnostics to inspect connection status, broker logs, and diagnostic observations.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-enamel-bright">Dashboard unreachable?</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-enamel-soft">Run <code>task ps</code> to check the services, then <code>task logs</code> for startup errors. Confirm port 8080 is available and run <code>task ready</code> to check readiness.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </Fragment>
            )}
          </CommandStep>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-12 max-w-[68ch] leading-relaxed text-enamel-muted">Stop the stack with <code>task down</code>. Read the <a class="link" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/production.md`}>Production deployment guide</a> for deployment requirements, broker TLS, and recovery limits.</p>
    </TrackSection>

    <footer class="mt-28 flex flex-col items-start justify-between gap-4 border-t border-track pt-8 text-sm text-enamel-muted sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
      <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} MCM contributors · Apache 2.0</p>
      <nav aria-label="Project resources" class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-3">
        <a class="hover:text-enamel-bright" href={repoURL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        <a class="hover:text-enamel-bright" href={`${repoURL}/issues`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issues</a>
        <a class="hover:text-enamel-bright" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">OpenAPI spec</a>
        <a class="hover:text-enamel-bright" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Security</a>
        <a class="hover:text-enamel-bright" href={`${base}system/`}>Brand system</a>
      </nav>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>
